WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.440
It writhes against the snow, red, raw, and
vicious.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.480
Too many mouths, too many limbs.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.240
Twitching and dripping.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.920
Once, it looked a lot like you, but now, it’s
something different entirely.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.680
If ever it escapes its bounds, it’ll rebuild
the whole world in its image.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:28.080
It is known and feared by everyone with sufficient
clearance at the SCP Foundation, and for good

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:35.360
reason: It’ll infect anyone and anything,
and a death sentence is preferable to infection.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.160
It is a disease that thinks.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.920
The crawling corruption.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.160
The Flesh That Hates.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.600
Or, if you fear its true name too much to
speak it, and find comfort in the categorization

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.280
and clinical eyes of the SCP Foundation: SCP-610.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.200
SCP-610 is a contagious skin disease, transmitted
by direct contact.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.560
Anyone infected with it suffers a horrific
mutation, turning them into fleshy, inhuman

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.000
monstrosities.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.960
These infected creatures will attack and infect
anyone nearby that isn’t also carrying SCP-610.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.840
This also happens to be “The Flesh” described
and adored by those following the twisted

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:24.160
religion of Sarkicism, a violent cult and
Group of Interest that worships flesh, corruption,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.440
and disease.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.800
And as the Foundation operatives tasked with
observing Groups of Interest know, Sarkicism

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.000
is a sect that directly&nbsp;
opposes the machine-revering&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.080
Church of the Broken God.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:42.000
And to understand the events of the tale known
to the SCP Foundation as Aftermath - the beginning

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.080
that leads to its brutal and world-changing
end - one must first understand the endless

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.200
conflict between these two groups.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.600
The Church of The Broken God is a religion
that the SCP Foundation has had a number of

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.680
encounters with over the years.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:03.120
Members of the Church share in the belief
that biological, flesh-based life is an inherently

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.680
wrong and evil abomination.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:11.280
They worship mechanization; the process of
making organic bodies something more mechanical

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.240
in nature.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:18.320
According to the beliefs of the Church, two
gods, Yaldabaoth and Mekhane, created humanity

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.040
together.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.560
Yaldabaoth was the god of flesh and animal
instinct, granting humans bodies.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.840
Meanwhile, the god of machine and intellect,
Mekhane, blessed man with the power of free

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:30.560
thought.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:36.240
As humankind developed machines, Yaldabaoth
became enraged that they were ignoring the

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:41.360
instincts she had given them and endeavored
to destroy the creations of man.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.200
As the Church’s legend goes, Mekhane acted
as humanity’s savior, and tried desperately

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.960
to stop Yaldabaoth.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.240
The god of machines shattered&nbsp;
himself, transforming&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.400
his body into a number of pieces to form a

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.560
cage for his fellow god.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.160
Fragments of Mekhane rained down on planet
Earth.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:05.040
Now, the Church of the Broken God believes
it is their duty to recover these missing

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:05.840
parts.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.560
There could potentially be hundreds of pieces
needed to rebuild Mekhane, and a number of

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.360
these happen to be catalogued SCPs that the&nbsp;

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.120
Foundation is either aware&nbsp;
of, or has in containment.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.000
Our story begins not with the long-awaited
return of Mekhane, the Broken God.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.480
Instead, it begins with a man.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.680
A Foundation foot soldier named Roderick Freeman.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.560
This is the story of Aftermath.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.720
In 2003, at the age of seventeen, Roderick’s
ambition was to join the US Navy and become

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.280
a member of the renowned Navy SEALs.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.320
After enlisting and completing three years
of rigorous training, he achieved his ambition,

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:49.040
only to climb even further, to heights he
never could have foreseen.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:55.360
In 2017, Roderick, now a SEAL, was recruited
by the SCP Foundation, after his skills and

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.400
aptitude caught the attention of their embedded
recruiters.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.600
He joined one of the Foundation’s MTFs,
or Mobile Task Forces, elite units that are

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.960
often sent in to directly deal with anomalous
threats.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.800
Specifically, Freeman became a member of MTF
Nu-7, also known by the codename “Hammer

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.840
Down” - the task force you call in when
literally nothing else can do the job.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.560
To bring Hammer Down onto the scene for anything
less than a potential XK is like swatting

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.120
a housefly with a nuclear warhead.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.040
So Roderick, a gung-ho soldier boy if there
ever was one, would fit right in.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.040
But what does this Mobile Task Force have
to do with all that talk about the Church

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.160
of the Broken God and the Flesh That Hates?

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.560
Well, after an incident that broke out in
the Irkutsk area of Russia, they were the

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.000
ones responsible for cleaning up the mess
left behind.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.480
According to Roderick’s account, a robot
the size of a small building was spotted in

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.440
this area during December 2018.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.560
This thirty foot tall robot had apparently
come to wipe out a rapidly-spreading disease.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:06.000
As you can probably guess, that disease was
SCP-610, the Flesh That Hates.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.640
At first, the Global Occult Coalition had
fired on the robot, launching a volley of

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.280
ballistic missiles in an attempt to take it
down.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.040
This move failed, the robot protecting itself
so that not even a piece of shrapnel could

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:19.680
hit it.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.960
It barely seemed fazed by the attack, and
went about destroying remnants of SCP-610

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.000
as it found them.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.840
Any infected with the Flesh were obliterated,
and when its job was done, the robot simply

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:32.480
left.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.320
Perhaps this wasn’t quite the grandiose
return for Mekhane that the Church of the

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.760
Broken God had envisioned for their deity,
but it was nevertheless the long-awaited return

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.800
they got.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:47.760
What had happened was what the SCP Foundation
called a Lifted Veil scenario.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:54.000
The truth was now out, the world would soon
be aware of the existence of anomalies.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.080
Afterwards, Freeman and the rest of Hammer
Down recovered a series of tablets that had

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.160
been left behind by Mekhane.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.840
Each one of them bore a simple, repeated phrase
in a variety of languages, just the words

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.760
“I will return”.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.360
A short time later, riots began to spark across
the world.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.520
It was a disaster too big for even the Foundation
to cover up.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.600
According to Roderick, multiple anomalous
groups such as the Serpent’s Hand and the

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.920
Chaos Insurgency had gone public.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:26.480
In Mexico, the Insurgency became involved
in illegal businesses that gave the cartels

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:31.200
an anomalous run for their ill-gotten money,
while members of the Serpent’s Hand used

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.760
the air of tension to incite riots.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:39.360
In short, everything was a mess, and this
eventually escalated to a full-scale civil

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.000
war in Mexico in 2021.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:47.760
During the build up to this, around 2019,
there was unrest around the world, and Mobile

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.160
Task Forces like Hammer Down were being deployed&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.360
to train alongside various&nbsp;
public safety organizations

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:58.640
- all in hopes of getting the world prepared
for the storm gathering all around them.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:04.080
The Insurgency and the Hand had revealed the
truth about anomalies to the world, and so

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:10.160
the Foundation’s MTFs were aiding law enforcement,
special forces and the like, readying them

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.480
to defend against the anomalous.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:18.640
In 2022, the Foundation finally decided to
intervene in the situation down in Mexico,

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:23.200
where the Chaos Insurgency and the Serpent’s
Hand had been causing disruption.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:28.240
Roderick Freeman was one of those sent to
Juarez, coming face to face with former cartel

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.040
members turned lackeys for the Insurgency.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:36.240
The Chaos Insurgency had been fighting with
the Foundation for decades, and knew all their

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.200
tactics.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:42.320
Combine that with the ferocity and brutality
of a lifelong cartel member and even the toughest

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.480
soldier is in for a fight.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:49.280
As it turns out, the fight wasn’t even the
worst part for our dedicated little soldier.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:54.320
While attempting to transport a person of
interest across the Texas/Mexico border, Roderick

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.800
and his squad were ambushed by a sniper.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:00.720
During the attack, Freeman received a wound
to his spine that left him paralyzed from

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:01.840
the hip down.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:05.840
However, even though the Foundation didn’t
like to admit it, the Church of the Broken

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.640
God was actually highly skilled in surgery.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.600
After all, they worshipped mechanization,&nbsp;

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.480
and would often augment&nbsp;
themselves using technology.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:19.280
Or, to use Roderick’s own words: “If you
wanted an iPhone in your skull in 2009, they

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:20.480
could've pulled it off.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:24.000
If you wanted to be able to turn the lights
on and off in your home by blinking, they

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.440
had an upgrade for that.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.920
If you lost the use of your legs because of
a sniper on a rooftop in Juarez, they had

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:30.880
you covered.”

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:35.120
Thanks to members of the Church, there had
been a new technological revolution since

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.560
the lifting of the Veil.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:41.520
By 2024, devices that felt like they were
twenty years more advanced than technology

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.000
should have been were now commonly available.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.920
So, that’s how Roderick Freeman was able
to walk again.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.560
However, the SCP Foundation refused to let&nbsp;

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:54.480
him return to duty, forcing&nbsp;
him into an administrative

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:55.120
role.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.800
Frustrated, he applied for a job as a containment
specialist.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:03.760
Meanwhile, the state of the world was constantly
changing, with the SCP Foundation handing

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.560
over safe anomalies to world governments.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:11.440
New divisions and departments were being formed
to deal with the containment of SCPs, there

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:17.120
was even an Anomaly Registration Program that
allowed people to call 911 to report dangerous

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.280
or life-threatening anomalies.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:24.000
Anyone exhibiting anomalous abilities could
now find doctors or therapists rather than

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.400
being carted off to a containment cell.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.520
In short, the Foundation’s days were numbered.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.640
However, this was not as idyllic as it sounds.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:36.480
According to Roderick, this should have been
a chance for the civil rights of anomalous

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:41.440
people to be respected - something the Serpent’s
Hand had been campaigning for since their

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:42.880
modern inception.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:47.600
Instead, it meant that anyone with anomalous
traits perceived to be dangerous was arrested

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.080
as threats to national security.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:54.720
Things were nowhere near as restrictive as
under the Foundation, the safer anomalies

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.640
could even have visits from family.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:01.600
But there was one boy, Thomas, whom Roderick
had to look after, remarking that he wasn’t

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.000
old enough to be kept in a containment setting.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:09.840
Little did Roderick know, the tests that were
being run on Thomas were keeping tabs on him.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:15.520
Somehow, the boy was able to use anomalous
abilities to watch where Roderick was at all

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:16.400
times.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:22.960
The SCP Foundation was finally disbanded in
2027, with the containment of anomalies becoming

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:26.080
the responsibility of the Global Coalition
Council.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.480
This organization had long been the official,
sanctioned counterpart to the more “off

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:36.080
the books” Foundation, despite their more
violent methods, but now the GOC was making

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:38.080
their work known to the public.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:43.040
But, with the Foundation gone, Roderick was
out of work, picking up odd jobs over the

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.400
next six years.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:49.760
There was widespread criticism of the SCP
Foundation and its dubious methods, the dark

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:52.800
things they’d done to keep anomalies contained.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:58.560
Civilians killed, entire populations given
memory wiping drugs to forget about SCPs,

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.280
the horrific treatment of D-Class personnel.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:06.000
A document containing details about these
practices and more was leaked, causing an

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:06.880
outcry.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:11.840
The SCP Foundation’s brutal methods were
declared to be crimes against humanity.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:15.840
Alongside this, paranoia about anomalies was
spreading.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:20.240
Governments were encouraging their citizens
to report paranormal happenings, and people

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.520
with anomalous traits were being registered
and arrested.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:28.400
In Roderick’s account, he says “When people
don't understand something, one of two things

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:32.320
will happen: they will try to understand it,
so they can use it for their own ends.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:37.280
Or, and this is far more likely, they will
grow afraid of it and try to destroy it.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:40.240
So, it was when humanity rediscovered anomalies.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:45.040
Former Foundation employees were declared
public enemy number one, with anomalous persons

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.160
at a close second.”

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:50.240
When former members of the Foundation began
to find themselves on trial by the United

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:53.520
Nations, the public began&nbsp;
executing any ex-Foundation&nbsp;

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.200
personnel they could find.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:59.840
At first, local police or even the National
Guard would intervene, but some eventually

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:02.960
started actively helping the vigilante mobs.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:08.320
There was nowhere for Roderick to hide, the
FBI even used the Unusual Incidents Unit to

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:10.880
track down the Foundation’s remaining members.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.440
Some had even been hired by the UIU to bring
in their former co-workers.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:20.480
And for anyone who knows how utterly useless
the Unusual Incidents Unit are, to be brought

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:25.200
in for execution by them is a truly humiliating
death.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:30.960
Unsure who to trust, Roderick turned to Agent
Leonard Wells, a man whose life he had once

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:31.680
saved.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:36.880
Meeting at a diner in Wisconsin, Leonard agreed
to smuggle Roderick to Russia for five thousand

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:40.560
dollars, getting him safely out of the FBI’s
jurisdiction.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:45.600
Freeman agreed, and was then led into an SUV
with three other men that he didn’t recognize.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.120
According to Leonard, they were just there
to help smuggle Roderick.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:53.920
The five of them drove to an isolated stretch
of road, only to stop.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.560
Something was terribly wrong.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:00.960
Leonard told Roderick to exit the car, claiming
that they would need to switch vehicles.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:05.600
As the SUV drove off, Leonard handed Roderick
a flashlight and told him to signal a nearby

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:06.880
grove of trees.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:07.360
And then…

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.880
According to a report, Roderick X. Freeman
was wanted by the US government for the actions

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:16.320
he was involved in during his time at the
SCP Foundation.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:20.720
He was believed to have been responsible for
human rights violations, and was picked up

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:24.160
by agents of the FBI’s Unusual Incidents
Unit.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:28.800
The report claimed that Roderick engaged the
UIU agents with a small firearm, although

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.520
he had reached out to Agent Leonard Wells
for help.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:36.960
Whether he was executed or tried to run away,
Roderick Freeman was shot and killed.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.000
But that was far from the worst part about
his death.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:45.040
Dying is bad enough, but witnessing death,
especially at a young age, is something that

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.200
can have a long-lasting effect.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.520
But who was there to see what happened?

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:53.120
Or rather, who could see without being there.

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:58.800
Thomas, the young anomalous boy Roderick had
been assigned to, had seen the whole thing.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:01.760
The world had changed, undeniably.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:07.200
It has been said that the Foundation dies
in the dark so that we can live in the light.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:12.000
But when that same light was turned to the
Foundation itself, it seemed they couldn’t

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.320
survive under its scrutiny, either.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:20.080
Whether the world is better or worse without
them is something only you can decide...

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.667
Now check out “SCP-5000 Why?

00:14:22.667 --> 00:14:28.640
- The Full Story Compilation” and “The
O5 Council Must Die SCP-001 - The Way It Ends

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:32.800
- Ouroboros Cycle” for more terrifying tales
from another timeline…

